te. **You Can Have Both** You do not have to choose between trusting yourself and being fair. You can do both at the exact same time. You can say to yourself: *"My family warned me, the news is crazy, and I've had bad experiences in the past. Because of that, I’m going to keep my eyes open and be cautious. BUT, I am going to wait and let this specific neighbor show me who he is before I make my final judgment."* That isn't doubting yourself. That is the ultimate form of self-trust. It means you are confident enough in your own real-time instincts that you don't need to pre-judge someone to stay safe. You can let them be an individual, knowing that if they *do* cross a line, your instincts will be right there to protect you.
